# assets/ is BOTH the game's authored asset tree AND the game dir we run retail
# out of: Jointops.exe, binkw32.dll, the retail runtime's own writes (game.cfg,
# player.sav, _filelog.txt, SYSDUMP.TXT, score.ini, ...), and the generated
# packaging output all land here beside our sources.
#
# So this is a BLANKET ignore with an explicit allowlist of the files we author.
# It is deliberately a list of NAMES WE ALLOW, never a list of names we exclude:
# a denylist here once let loose retail copies slip into a commit. Adding an
# asset means adding a line, and that is the point -- it forces the call to be
# made consciously rather than by a wildcard that also sweeps in retail data.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# --- Boot: the fatal set + menu strings (RTXT .bin) ---
!/gameerr.bin
!/gametext.bin
!/vmacros.bin
!/keyhelp.bin
!/menutxt.bin

# --- Pre-archive error text: read loose before any mount ---
# Retail reads this before a single archive is open, so it can never live inside one; without
# it the dialog degrades to "Error: Unable to open EARLYERR.TXT"
# [orig: Game_ShowEarlyError @ 0x4a68a0]. Lines 3 and 4 are the no-archives and
# missing-gameerr.bin messages. CRLF, like every authored text file here.
!/earlyerr.txt

# --- Music: the two script + bank pairs, loaded by name ---
!/menumus.sbf
!/menumus.bin
!/gamemus.sbf
!/gamemus.bin

# --- Fonts: the boot face set ---
# Retail looks these up by these exact names off a hardcoded table; a missing one is a null
# slot that draws nothing at all [orig: HUD_InitAllFonts @ 0x51ee20].
!/Arial12b.fnt
!/Arial14n.fnt
!/Arial14b.fnt
!/Arial16n.fnt
!/Arial16b.fnt
!/Impac22b.fnt
!/Impac38b.fnt

# --- Definitions (plain text) ---
!/items.def
!/weapon.def
!/ammo.def

# --- Menus + stylesheet + cursor ---
!/main.mnu
!/mp.mnu
!/sp.mnu
!/menu_style.mns
!/newarow1.tga

# --- The mnml map: mission, terrain, environment, companions, source art ---
!/mnml.bms
!/mnml.trn
!/mnml.env
!/mnml.bin
!/mnml.dbf
!/mnml.lwf
!/mnml.pcx
!/mnml_c.tga
!/mnml_dm.tga
!/mnml.cpt
!/mnml_dc1.tga
!/mnml_dc2.tga
!/mnml_dc3.tga
!/mnml_dmd.tga
!/mnml_d1.tga
!/mnml_t.tga
!/mnml_m.pcx
!/mnml_f.pcx

# --- Shaders: the authored .fx set (SCR-wrapped; sources in tests/fixtures/fx/) ---
# The boot shader precompile enumerates .fx through PFF directory walks and the
# effect loader accepts only the 'SCR',0x01 container (key 0xA55B1EED)
# [orig: ScriptFile_LoadAndDecrypt @ 0x5AE060] -- without these the FP viewmodel
# and every skinned draw silently fall back to fixed-function. minimal_fx_gen
# guards that each artifact byte-equals wrap(source) and that no stray .fx
# rides beside them.
!/_baseinc.fx
!/_vsshared.fx
!/_vsskshared.fx
!/_psshared.fx
!/_tdepth.fx
!/_tskin.fx
!/_ffp.fx
!/phongt.fx
!/skbasic.fx
!/skbdifft2.fx
!/skbdiffo.fx
!/skbdiffo2.fx
!/skbphongt.fx
!/skbphongo.fx

# --- Models + textures we author: the house (items.def 108001, placed in mnml) ---
# assets/house.3di is the fixtures/threedi/synth `house` recipe minted again by
# minimal_3di_gen (one recipe, two byte-guarded copies); the three flat-colour
# swatch textures it names are minted beside it.
!/house.3di
!/wall.tga
!/roof.tga
!/wood.tga

# --- Models + textures authored in Godot (sources under godot/authoring/<name>/) ---
# Exported by the opennova_model addon through the parity writer and re-exported
# + byte-compared by godot/tests/model_export_guard_test.gd. The crate (items.def
# 108002, placed in mnml) is the first: a Blender box through Godot's glTF importer.
!/crate.3di
!/crate.tga
# The player body and head on the retail reset clip's 20-row rig (DT1RST.BAD bone
# order and pivots, until our own clips exist; ADR 0046 decision 5): the avatar
# combo AVATARS.DEF names, minted from godot/authoring/person and person_hd.
!/person.3di
!/person.tga
!/person_hd.3di
!/person_hd.tga
# The first-person rifle (rigid, 45 parts) and arms (skinned, 38 rows) on the
# retail rAKM_RST.bad rig with AKM_1st's pivots (the arms share the rifle's
# table; ArmsG's ground proxy ends theirs), minted from godot/authoring/akm and
# arms: weapon.def's GFX1 and the AVATARS.DEF arms. The type-5 normal slots
# take a flat 32 bpp TGA (the normal rides the alpha, retail's flat_N.tga form).
!/akm.3di
!/akm.tga
!/akm_n.tga
!/brass.tga
!/arms.3di
!/arms.tga
!/arms_n.tga

# --- Definitions we author with the engine writers ---
# The avatar table: one head, one body, the arms, one nationality per
# alignment. Minted by minimal_avatars_gen (--write).
!/AVATARS.DEF

# --- Clips we author in Godot (sources: godot/authoring/<name>/*_clips.tres) ---
# Projected from the rigs' Animations by the opennova_model addon through the
# .bad/.adm writers and re-exported + byte-compared by
# godot/tests/clip_export_guard_test.gd (ADR 0047). The body set on person's
# twenty rows (person.adm: reset, idle, the eight walk / crouch-walk / crawl
# directions, run, jog, crouch, prone, jump, death and reload, every death key
# on the one fall; failsafe.bad is the reset under the name every mission
# start loads) and the first-person rifle set on the 46 rAKM rows (akm.adm:
# reset, idle, fire, reload; the rifle's 45 parts and the arms' 38 rows read
# their own prefix).
!/failsafe.bad
!/pers_crouch.bad
!/pers_crwlb.bad
!/pers_crwlbl.bad
!/pers_crwlbr.bad
!/pers_crwlf.bad
!/pers_crwlfl.bad
!/pers_crwlfr.bad
!/pers_crwll.bad
!/pers_crwlr.bad
!/pers_cwlkb.bad
!/pers_cwlkbl.bad
!/pers_cwlkbr.bad
!/pers_cwlkf.bad
!/pers_cwlkfl.bad
!/pers_cwlkfr.bad
!/pers_cwlkl.bad
!/pers_cwlkr.bad
!/pers_death.bad
!/pers_idle.bad
!/pers_jog.bad
!/pers_jump.bad
!/pers_prone.bad
!/pers_reload.bad
!/pers_run.bad
!/pers_walkb.bad
!/pers_walkbl.bad
!/pers_walkbr.bad
!/pers_walkf.bad
!/pers_walkfl.bad
!/pers_walkfr.bad
!/pers_walkl.bad
!/pers_walkr.bad
!/person.adm
!/person_rst.bad
!/akm.adm
!/akm_fire.bad
!/akm_idle.bad
!/akm_reload.bad
!/akm_rst.bad


# --- TEMPORARY: the retail bring-up set (committed 2026-08-31, to be replaced) ---
# These are RETAIL Joint Operations bytes: the two definition tables the
# bring-up set README.md describes (the models, textures, avatar table, clips
# and anim defs are ours now, above). Committed by explicit decision so the
# minimal set runs (and ships) from a fresh checkout; every line is deleted
# as our own writer-produced replacement lands. Names stay individually
# listed on purpose: removing one is the same conscious call as adding one.
# retail defs
!/charattr.def
!/SndProf.def
